 34CL c  Compiled by L. Hixson (FRIB, MSU), January 24, 2023                    
 34CL c  Edited by J. Chen (FRIB, MSU), August 31, 2023                         
 34CL c  2020Ia02: pure {+34}Ar samples were produced using a 30 MeV/nucleon    
 34CL2c  {+35}Cl beam from the K500 superconducting cyclotron at Texas A&M      
 34CL3c  University on a liquid-nitrogen cooled hydrogen in a gas cell. Fully   
 34CL4c  stripped reaction ejectiles were separated and identified using the    
 34CL5c  MARS recoil separator and transported to the counting station. |g rays 
 34CL6c  were detected with a HPGe detector and positrons were detected with a  
 34CL7c  scintillator. Measured E|g, E|b, |b|g-coin. Deduced levels, decay      
 34CL8c  branching ratios, log {Ift}, Gamow-Teller strengths. Comparisons with  
 34CL9c  available data and shell-model calculations.                           
